  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="d75d72ae-c9fc-4073-853e-388d1687960e" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="d6f8070d-51ee-4e35-9188-c3c9a9779198" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="No; Her solution does not make both equations true." data-solution-options="[&quot;yes; Her solution makes both equations true.&quot;, &quot;No; Her solution does not make both equations true.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>1. Lin is solving this system of equations: </para>
      <para>\( \begin {cases} 6x-5y=34\\3x+2y=8 \end {cases} \)</para>
      <para>She starts by rearranging the second equation to isolate the \(y\) variable: \( y = 4 - 1.5x \). She then substitutes the expression \(4 - 1.5x\) for \( y \) in the first equation, as shown:</para>
      <para> \( 6x-5(4-1.5x)=34 \)</para>
      <para>\( -1.5x=54 \)</para>
      <para>\( y=4-1.5x \)</para>
      <para>\( y=4-1.5 \cdot(-36) \)</para>
      <para>\( y=58 \)</para>
      <para>Does Lin’s solution of \((-36, 58)\) makes both equations in the system true?</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! No; Her solution does not make both equations true.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.3.2.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="fc2e0fa3-9cd1-4dff-987c-17aa1afa8afd" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="Lin made a multiplication error. The correct answer is \(x = 4\) and \(y = -2\), or \((4,-2).\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;Lin made a multiplication error. The correct answer is \\(x = 4\\) and \\(y = -2\\), or \\((4,-2).\\)&quot;, &quot;Lin made a multiplication error. The correct answer is \\(x = 9\\) and \\(y = 4\\), or (9,4).&quot;, &quot;Lin made an addition error. The correct answer is \\(x = 0\\) and \\(y = 4\\), or (0,4).&quot;, &quot;Lin’s solution of (-36, 58) is correct.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>2. Which of the following is true of Lin’s solution?</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Lin made a multiplication error. The correct answer is x = 4 and y = -2, or (4,-2).</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.3.2.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </div>
</div>
<para>In 3 - 9, solve the systems of equations by substitution.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="c990ad58-9eaf-456c-aea8-62ff441d6b9d" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="a42eaa70-a2fc-4597-8102-6b37c1b48ad6" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((1,−4)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((−1,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,−2) \\)&quot;, &quot;\\((1,−4)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((2,6)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>3. \(\left\{\begin{array}{l}2x+y=-2\\3x-y=7\end{array}\right.\)</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! (1,−4)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 2.3.3 and 2.3.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="527afbcf-da67-43bf-a980-73f4d3ab4824" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((−3,2)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((−6,1)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((2,0) \\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,3)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((−3,2)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>4. \(\left\{\begin{array}{l}x-3y=-9\\2x+5y=4\end{array}\right.\)</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! (−3,2)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 2.3.3 and 2.3.4.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="6193e47f-ea4f-4dce-ad7b-26c2028856de" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((1,4)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((1,4)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,7) \\)&quot;, &quot;\\((2,1)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((−3,0)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>5. \(\left\{\begin{array}{l}-2x+2y=6\\2y=-6x+14\end{array}\right.\)</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! (1,4)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 2.3.3 and 2.3.4.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="96fbcd3b-ef40-4cf3-b0a4-0f88ccb60448" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((−5,4)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((5,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,2) \\)&quot;, &quot;\\((−1,1)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((−5,4)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>6. \(\left\{\begin{array}{l}3x+4y=1\\y=-\frac25x+2\end{array}\right.\)</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! (−5,4)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para> Try again. Revisit activities 2.3.3 and 2.3.4.

      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="ade4892d-a5f1-4d15-b82a-1e79e6d4d8c9" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((0,10)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((2,2)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,10)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((−4,8)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((4,12)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>7. \(\left\{\begin{array}{l}3x+y=10\\x-2y=-20\end{array}\right.\)</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! (0,10)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para> Try again. Revisit activities 2.3.3 and 2.3.4.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q8-->
  <exercise data-content-id="59b0d4f7-31f5-453a-b7e2-1c74c33f9fda" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((4,−2)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((6,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((2,1) \\)&quot;, &quot;\\((4,−2)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,4)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>8. \(\left\{\begin{array}{l}y=x-6\\y=-\frac32x+4\end{array}\right.\)</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! (4,−2)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para> Try again. Revisit activities 2.3.3 and 2.3.4.

      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q9-->
  <exercise data-content-id="401e6494-8f33-4e4d-b593-16e163d0cb2b" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((4,0)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((12,1)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((4,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((−4,1)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((−4,−1)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>9. \(\left\{\begin{array}{l}2x-16y=8\\-x-8y=-4\end{array}\right.\)</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! (4,0)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para> Try again. Revisit activities 2.3.3 and 2.3.4.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q10-->
  <exercise data-content-id="16baa37a-12b3-4828-97a4-45ccf7b841bd" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((3,4)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((0,6)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((−2,0)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((3,4)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((6,2)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>10. \(\left\{\begin{array}{l}y=-\frac23x+6\\2x-y=2\end{array}\right.\)</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! (3,4)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 2.3.3 and 2.3.4.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q11-->
  <exercise data-content-id="658cf1ee-cc3d-4df0-ba52-cd6e1eac9d07" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\((1,-2)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\((1,-2)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((0,1)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((4,-3)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((-5,0)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>11. Tyler and Han are trying to solve this system by substitution:</para>
      <para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{l}x+3y=-5\\9x+3y=3\end{array}\right.\)</para>
      <para> Tyler's first step is to isolate x in the first equation to get \(x = -5 - 3y.\)</para>
      <para>Han's first step is to isolate 3y in the first equation to get \(3y = -5 - x.\)</para>
      <para>Solve using both methods to show that both first steps can be used to solve the system and will yield the same solution.</para>
      <para>What is the solution to the system?</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! (1,-2)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 2.3.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
